{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00983",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 2.57,
      "end_seconds": 17.08,
      "duration_seconds": 14.51,
      "text": "Hi, quickly please, I'm on my lunch break. I slipped on ice this morning on the way to the car and landed on my left hand. My wrist is killing me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.7,
      "end_seconds": 24.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "Thanks for coming straight in. Describe the pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 27.45,
      "end_seconds": 36.15,
      "duration_seconds": 8.7,
      "text": "Sharp, right at the base of the thumb side, worse if I try to turn the hand over."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.76,
      "end_seconds": 43.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "Can you move your fingers? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 47.44,
      "end_seconds": 50.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "Yes, I can wiggle them. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 53.55,
      "end_seconds": 55.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "Any numbness or tingling?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 58.51,
      "end_seconds": 60.32,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "No. None."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 62.65,
      "end_seconds": 66.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "Any other medical conditions I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 70.15,
      "end_seconds": 71.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "Just asthma."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 82.82,
      "end_seconds": 94.21,
      "duration_seconds": 11.39,
      "text": "Let me take your numbers. Pulse 82, blood pressure 124 over 80, temperature 36.7, oxygen 99 percent, breathing 16."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.93,
      "end_seconds": 99.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "Is that okay? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 103.27,
      "end_seconds": 119.82,
      "duration_seconds": 16.55,
      "text": "Fine. Now, I want to explain what I'm thinking. When someone falls onto an outstretched hand, one of the small bones in the wrist, or the end of the forearm bone, can crack. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.21,
      "end_seconds": 125.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "Is it broken? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.33,
      "end_seconds": 143.49,
      "duration_seconds": 15.16,
      "text": "I can't say without an X-ray. But with this kind of fall and pain on the thumb side, I think it's possibly a fracture of the wrist."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 147.17,
      "end_seconds": 150.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "Great. I've got a presentation tomorrow. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.02,
      "end_seconds": 165.73,
      "duration_seconds": 11.71,
      "text": "I understand. The X-ray will answer the question quickly. I'd like to arrange an X-ray of the wrist, today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 168.97,
      "end_seconds": 170.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.89,
      "text": "Where? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.75,
      "end_seconds": 179.13,
      "duration_seconds": 5.38,
      "text": "Radiology is down the corridor. They'll fit you in. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.41,
      "end_seconds": 186.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "Fine. And in the meantime? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.6,
      "end_seconds": 201.68,
      "duration_seconds": 11.08,
      "text": "Keep it elevated on a pillow, and use a cold pack wrapped in a cloth for twenty minutes at a time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 205.04,
      "end_seconds": 206.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.53,
      "text": "Okay. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.44,
      "end_seconds": 217.83,
      "duration_seconds": 8.39,
      "text": "Don't use the hand to lift anything. A sling would help for a few hours."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 221.02,
      "end_seconds": 223.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "I'll ask the nurse. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.48,
      "end_seconds": 233.46,
      "duration_seconds": 6.98,
      "text": "For the pain, you can take paracetamol, nothing more than the label says. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 236.82,
      "end_seconds": 238.2,
      "duration_seconds": 1.38,
      "text": "Right. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.32,
      "end_seconds": 248.08,
      "duration_seconds": 6.76,
      "text": "Take the X-ray result back to the front desk, and they'll find me. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 251.25,
      "end_seconds": 255.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "Will you look at it today? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 258.8,
      "end_seconds": 267.66,
      "duration_seconds": 8.86,
      "text": "Yes. If the X-ray shows a fracture, I'll refer you to the fracture clinic right away for a cast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 271.51,
      "end_seconds": 275.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.31,
      "text": "Okay. And if it doesn't? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.93,
      "end_seconds": 285.32,
      "duration_seconds": 6.39,
      "text": "Then we'll treat it as a sprain, with a wrist splint. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 288.88,
      "end_seconds": 291.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "That I can handle. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.31,
      "end_seconds": 299.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "Good luck with the presentation. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 302.75,
      "end_seconds": 305.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "Thanks. I'll need it. ~"
    }
  ]
}
